// Members after `.` (M5, §13.1): the value types on the left are for all instance:
// 
//  
// entity fields from struct and all extensions
//,
//), размер массива, функции через точку `a.f(b) ≡ f(a, b)` (§4.5);
// конструкции (for, while, try) — синтаксис, не члены. Функция с нетипизированным
// первым параметром — только если в каком-то экземпляре он получал этот тип.
// program: editor_members.vish
open_view module
// expect: kind="type" text="point"
// aggregate: struct fields and expansion function, then functions through a point
pointer 1 @.sum 1 1
key 1 \s 2
// expect: items=⏎  name="sum" kind="функция" detail="()"
// expect: name="x" kind="поле" detail="f64 — point"
// expect: name="y" kind="поле" detail="f64 — point"
// total(xs) is not called with point - not offered
// expect-not: name="total"
// expect-not: name="for"
// expect-not: name="while"
key 1 Escape
// Array: size, function through point; no field
pointer 1 @.size 1 1
key 1 \s 2
// expect: items=⏎  name="size" kind="поле" detail="i64 — array<f64>"
// total(xs) is called with array<f64>
// expect: name="total" kind="функция" detail="()"
// expect-not: name="x"
key 1 Escape
// filter
pointer 1 @.size 1 5
key 1 Backspace
key 1 Backspace
key 1 Backspace
// expect: курсор:   print(xs.s‸);
// expect: items=⏎  name="size"
// text - hole (`xs.`): type is taken by name on the left, list opens at the point
key 1 Backspace
// expect: курсор:   print(xs.‸);
// expect: kind="n_hole"
// expect: items=⏎  name="size"
// Take - again member, no hole, no mistakes
key 1 Enter
// expect: курсор:   print(xs.size‸);
// expect-not: n_hole
// expect-not: kind="error"
